te(6650.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"2C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>meaning it is independent of the mass number <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.697ex\" height=\"1.62ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 750 716\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>.</p></p>\n\n<p>Thus, the correct option is:</p>\n<p>Option B: Independent of A.</p>","qKey":"m9dn5osv","paperKey":"jee-main-2025-online-8th-april-evening-shift","exam":"jee-main","questions":[{"question_id":"m9dn5osv","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2025 (Online) 8th April Evening Shift","year":2025,"subject":"physics","chapter":"atoms-and-nuclei","chapterGroup":"modern-physics","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>For a nucleus of mass number A and radius R, the mass density of nucleus can be represented as</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.154ex\" height=\"2.211ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -977.1 1394.1 977.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(783,365.5) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-T